{
  "title": "Dua Kumayl",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ \nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اَسْاَلُكَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ الَّتِيْ وَسِعَتْ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ \nALLAAHUMMA INNI AS-ALOKA BERAH’MATEKAL LATEE WASEA’T KULLA SHAY-IN \nO Allah! I ask You by Your mercy, which encompasses all things\nوَ بِقُوَّتِكَ الَّتِيْ قَهَرْتَ بِهَا كُلَّ شَيْءٍ \nWA BE-QUWWATEKAL LATEE QAHARTA BEHAA KULLA SHAY-IN\nAnd by Your strength, through which You dominate all things,\nوَ خَضَعَ لَهَا كُلُّ شَيْءٍ \nWA KHAZA-A’ LAHAA KULLO SHAY-IN \nAnd to which all things submit\nوَ ذَلَّ لَهَا كُلُّ شَيْءٍ \nWA ZALLA LAHAA KULLO SHAY-IN\nAnd before which all things are humble;\nوَ بِجَبَرُوْتِكَ الَّتِيْ غَلَبْتَ بِهَا كُلَّ شَيْءٍ \nWA BE-JABAROOTEKAL LATEE GHALABTA BEHAA KULLA SHAY-IN \nAnd by Your invincibility through which You overwhelm all things,\nوَ بِعِزَّتِكَ الَّتِيْ لَا يَقُوْمُ لَهَا شَيْءٌ \nWA BE-I’ZZATEKAL LATEE LAA YAQOOMO LAHAA SHAY-UN\nAnd by Your might, which nothing can resist:\nوَ بِعَظَمَتِكَ الَّتِيْ مَلَاَتْ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ \nWA BE-A’ZAMATEKAL LATEE MALA-AT KULLA SHAY-IN \nAnd by Your grandeur, which prevails upon all things;\nوَ بِسُلْطانِكَ الَّذي عَلٰي كُلَّ شَيْءٍ \nWA BE-SULTAANEKAL LAZEE A’LAA KULLA SHAY-IN\nby Your authority, which is exercised over all things:\nوَ بِوَجْهِكَ الْبَاقِيْ بَعْدَ فَنَاءِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ \nWA BE-WAJHEKAL BAAQI BA’DA FANAAA-E KULLE SHAY-IN \nAnd by Your face, which shall endure after the annihilation of all things.\nوَ بِاَسْمَائِكَ الَّتِيْ مَلَاَتْ اَرْكَانَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ \nWA BE-ASMAAA-EKAL LATEE MALA-AT ARKAANA KULLE SHAY-IN\nAnd by Your Names, which have occupied the being of all things:\nوَ بِعِلْمِكَ الَّذِيْ اَحَاطَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ \nWA BE-I’LMEKAL LAZEE AHAATA BE KULLE SHAY-IN \nAnd by Your knowledge, which pervades all things:\nوَ بِنُوْرِ وَجْهِكَ الَّذِيْ اَضَاءَ لَهٗ كُلُّ شَيْءٍ \nWA BE-NOORE WAJHEKAL LAZEE AZAA-A LAHU KULLO SHAY-IN \nAnd by the light of Your countenance, which illuminates all things\nيَا نُوْرُ يَا قُدُّوْسُ \nYAA NOORO YAA QUDDOOSO \nO Light! O All-Holy! \nيَا اَوَّلَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ \nYAA AWWALAL AWWALEENA \nO You who existed before the foremost! \nوَ يَا آخِرَ الْآخِرِيْنَ \nWA YAA AAKHERAL AAKHEREENA \nO You who shall exist after the last!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِيْ تَهْتِكُ الْعِصَمَ \nALLAAHUM-MAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TAHTEKUL E’SAMA \nO Allah! Forgive me those sins which tear apart safeguards!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِيْ تُنْزِلُ النِّقَمَ \nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TUNZELUN NEQAMA \nO Allah! Forgive me those sins which draw down adversities!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِيْ تُغَيِّرُ النِّعَمَ \nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TOGHAYYERUN NE-A’M\nO Allah! Forgive me those sins which change divine favours (into disfavours)!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِيْ تَحْبِسُ الدُّعَاءَ \nALLAAAHUMMAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TAHBESUD DOA\nO Allah! Forgive me those sins which hold back supplication!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِيْ تَقْطَعُ الرَّجَآءَ \nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TAQTA-U’R RAJAAA \nO Allah! Forgive me those sins which draw down tribulation!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِيْ تُنْزِلُ الْبَلَاءَ \nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TUNZELUL BALAA\nO Allah! Forgive me those sins which suppress hopes!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِيْ كُلَّ ذَنْبٍ اَذْنَبْتُهٗ \nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LEE KULLA ZAMBIN AZNABTAHU\nO Allah! Forgive me every sin I have committed \nوَ كُلَّ خَطِيْئَة اَخْطَاْتُهَا \nWA KULLA KHATEEATIN AKHTAATOHAA \nand every mistake I have made!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَيْكَ بِذِكْرِكَ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ATAQARRABO ELAYKA BE ZIKREKA \nO Allah! Verily I seek nearness to You through remembrance of You.\nوَ اَسْتَشْفِعُ بِكَ اِلٰى نَفْسِكَ \nWA ASTASHFEO’ BEKA ELAA NAFSEKA \nAnd I seek intercession from You with Yourself,\nوَ اَسْاَلُكَ بِجُوْدِكَ اَنْ تُدْنِيَنِيْ مِنْ قُرْبِكَ \nWA AS-ALOKA BE JOODEKA AN TUDNEYANI MIN QURBEKA \nAnd I ask You through Your benevolence to bring me near to Your proximity,\nوَ اَنْ تُوْزِعَنِيْ شُكْرَكَ \nWA AN TOOZE-A’NI SHUKRAKA \nAnd to provide me with gratitude toward You\nوَ اَنْ تُلْهِمَنِيْ ذِكْرَكَ \nWA AN TULHEMANI ZIKRAKA \nAnd to inspire me with Your remembrance.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَسْاَلُكَ سُؤَالَ خَاضِعٍ مُتَذَلِّلٍ خَاشِعٍ \nALLAAHUMMA INNI AS-ALOKA SO-AALA KHAAZE-I’N MOTAZ’ALLELIN KHAASHEI’N \nO Allah! Verily I ask You with the asking of a submissive, abased and lowly man\nاَنْ تُسَامِحَنِيْ وَ تَرْحَمَنِيْ \nAN TOSAAMEHANEE WA TARHAMANEE \nTo show me forbearance and to have mercy on me\nوَ تَجْعَلَنِيْ بِقِسْمِكَ رَاضِيًا قَانِعًا \nWA TAJ-A’LANI BE-QISMEKA RAAZEYAN QAANEA’N \nAnd to make me satisfied and content with Your appointment\nوَ فِيْ جَمِيْعِ الْاَحْوَالِ مُتَوَاضِعًا \nWA FEE JAMEE-I’L AHWAALE MOTAWAAZEA’N \nAnd [make me] humble in every state.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ اَسْاَلُكَ سُؤَالَ مَنِ اشْتَدَّتْ فَاقَتُهٗ \nALLAAHUMMA WA AS-ALOKA SO-AALA MANISH TADDAT FAAQATOHU \nO Allah! I ask You the question of one whose indigence is extreme.\nوَ اَنْزَلَ بِكَ عِنْدَ الشَّدَائِدِ حَاجَتَهٗ \nWA ANZALA BEKA I’NDASH SHADAAEDE HAAJATAHU \nAnd who has stated to You in difficulties his need\nوَ عَظُمَ فِيْمَا عِنْدَكَ رَغْبَتُهٗ\nWA A’ZOMA FEEMA I’NDAKA RAGHBATOHU \nAnd whose desire for what is with You has become great.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ عَظُمَ سُلْطَانُكَ \nALLAAHUMMA A’ZOMA SULTAANOKA \nO Allah! Great is Your kingdom \nوَ عَلَا مَكَانُكَ \nWA A’LAA MAKAANOKA \nand exalted is Your greatness;\nوَ خَفِيَ مَكْرُكَ وَ ظَهَرَ اَمْرُكَ \nWA KHAFEYA MAKROKA WA ZAHARA AMROKA \nAnd Your plan is hidden. Your authority is manifest.\nوَ غَلَبَ قَهْرُكَ وَ جَرَتْ قُدْرَتُكَ \nWA GHALABA QAHROKA WA JARAT QUDRATOKA \nAnd Your domination is overwhelming. Your power is unhindered\nوَ لَا يُمْكِنُ الْفِرَارُ مِنْ حُكُوْمَتِكَ \nWA LAA YUMKENUL FERAARO MIN HOKOOMATEKA \nAnd escape from Your governance is impossible.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا اَجِدُ لِذُنُوْبِيْ غَافِرًا \nALLAAHUMMA LAA AJEDO LEZONOOBI GHAAFERAN \nO Allah! I find no forgiver of my sins.\nوَ لَا لِقَبَائِحِيْ سَاتِرًا \nWA LAA LE QABAAEHI SAATERAN \nNor concealer of my ugly acts\nوَ لَا لِشَيْءٍ مِنْ عَمَلِيَ الْقَبِيْحِ بِالْحَسَنِ مُبَدِّلًا غَيْرَكَ \nWA LAA LESHAY-IN MIN A’MALEYAL QABEEHE BIL HASANE MOBADDELAN GHAYRAKA \nNor transformer of any of my ugly acts into good acts but You\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ وَ بِحَمْدِكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA WA BE- HAMDEKA \nThere is no god but You! Glory and Praise be to You!\nظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِيْ وَ تَجَرَّاْتُ بِجَهْلِيْ \nZALAMTO NAFSEE WA TAJARRAATO BE JAHLEE\nI have wronged myself. And I have been audacious in my ignorance\nوَ سَكَنْتُ اِلٰى قَدِيْمِ ذِكْرِكَ لِيْ وَ مَنِّكَ عَلَيَّ \nWA SAKANTO ELAA QADEEME ZIKREKA LEE WA MANNEKA A’LAYYA \nAnd I have depended upon Your constant remembrance of me and Your favour toward me.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مَوْلَايَ كَمْ مِنْ قَبِيْحٍ سَتَرْتَهٗ \nALLAAHUMMA MAWLAAYA KAM MIN QABEEHIN SATARTAHU \nO Allah! O my Protector! How many ugly things You have concealed!\nوَ كَمْ مِنْ فَادِحٍ مِنَ الْبَلَاءِ اَقَلْتَهٗ \nWA KAM MIN FAADEHIN MENAL BALAAAE AQALTAHU \nHow many burdensome tribulations You have abolished!\nوَ كَمْ مِّنْ عِثَارٍ وَّ قَيْتَهٗ \nWA KAM MIN ESAARIN WAQAYTAHU \nAnd how many stumbles You have prevented!\nوَ كَمْ مِّنْ مَكْرُوْهٍ دَفَعْتَهٗ \nWA KAM MIN MAKROOHIN DAFA’-TAHU \nAnd how many ordeals You have repelled!\nوَ كَمْ مِّنْ ثَنَآءٍ جَمِيْلٍ لَّسْتُ اَهْلًا لَهٗ نَشَرْتَهٗ \nWA KAM MIN SANAAA-IN JAMEELIN LASTO AHLAN LAHU NASHARTAHU \nAnd how much beautiful praise, for which I was unworthy. You have spread abroad!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ عَظُمَ بَلَآئِيْ \nALLAAHUMMA A’ZOMA BALAAA-EE \nO Allah! My tribulation is tremendous.\nوَ اَفْرَطَ بِيْ سُوْٓ ءُ حَالِيْ وَ قَصُرَتْ بِيْ اَعْمَالِيْ \nWA AFRATA BEE SOOO-O H’AALEE WA QASORAT BEE A’AMAALEE \nAnd my bad state is excessive. And my good acts are inadequate.\nوَ قَعَدَتْ بِيْ اَغْلَالِىْ \nWA QA-A’DAT BI AGHLAALEE \nAnd my fetters have tied me down, \nوَ حَبَسَنِيْ عَنْ نَفْعِيْ بُعْدُ اَمَلِيْ \nWA HABASANEE A’N NAF-I’I BO’DO AMALEE \nand my far-fetched hopes have held me back from gaining (by good deals)\nوَ خَدَعَتْنِيْ الدُّنْيَا بِغُرُوْرِهَا وَ نَفْسِيْ بِجِنَايَتِهَا وَ مِطَالِيْ \nWA KHAD-A’TNID DUNYAA BE GHOROOREHA WA NAFSEE BE JENAAYATEHAA WA METAALEE \nAnd this world with its delusions, my own soul with its offences and my delay have deceived me.\nيَا سَيِّدِيْ فَاَسْاَلُكَ بِعِزَّتِكَ اَنْ لَا يَحْجُبَ عَنْكَ دُعَآئِيْ سُوْٓءُ عَمَلِيْ وَ فِعَالِيْ \nYAA SAYYEDEE FA-ASALOKA BE I’ZZATEKA AN LAA YAHJOBA A’NKA DOA’A-EE SOOO-O A’MALEE WA FE-A’ALEE \nO my Master! So I ask You by Your Might not to let my evil works and acts veil my supplication from You.\nوَ لَا تَفْضَحْنِيْ بِخَفِيِّ مَا اطَّلَعْتَ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ سِرِّىْ \nWA LAA TAFZAH’NI BE KHAFEEYYE MAT-TLA’TA A’LAYHE MIN SIRREE \nAnd not to disgrace me through the hidden things You know of my secrets\nوَ لَا تُعَاجِلْنِيْ بِالْعُقُوْبَةِ عَلٰى مَا عَمِلْتُهٗ فِيْ خَلَوَاتِيْ \nWA LAA TOA’AJILNEE BIL O’QOOBATE A’LAA MAA A’MILTOHU FEE KHALAWAATEE \nAnd not to hasten me to punishment for what I have done in private:\nمِنْ سُوْٓ ءِ فِعْلِيْ وَ اِسَآئَتِيْ \nMIN SOOO-E FE’LEE WA ESAA-ATEE \nMy evil acts in secrecy and my misdeeds\nوَ دَوَامِ تَفْرِيْطِيْ وَ جَهَالَتِيْ \nWA DAWAAME TAFREETEE WA JAHAALATEE \nAnd my continuous negligence and my ignorance\nوَ كَثْرَةِ شَهْوَاتِيْ وَ غَفْلَتِيْ \nWA KASRATE SHAWAATEE WA GHAFLATEE \nAnd my manifold passions ami my forgetfulness.\nوَ كُنِ اللّٰهُمَّ بِعِزَّتِكَ لِيْ فِيْ كُلِّ الْاَحْوَالِ رَؤُوْفًا \nWA KONIL LAAHUMMA BE I’ZZATEKA LEE FEE KULLIL AH’WAALE RAOOFAN \nAnd by Your Might. O Allah! Be kind to me in all states \nوَّ عَلَيَّ فِيْ جَمِيْعِ الْاُمُوْرِ عَطُوْفًا \nWA A’LAYYA FEE JAMEE-I’L OMOORE A’TOOFAN \nand be gracious to me in all affairs!\nاِلٰهِيْ وَ رَبِّيْ مَنْ لِيْ غَيْرُكَ اَسْاَلُهٗ كَشْفَ ضُرِّيْ وَ النَّظَرَ فِيْ اَمْرِيْ \nELAAHEE WA RABBEE MAN LEE GHAYROKA ASALOHU KASHFA ZURREE WAN NAZARA FEE AMREE \nMy God and my Lord! Have I any but You from whom to ask removal of my affliction and regard for my affairs!\nاِلٰهِيْ وَ مَوْلَايَ اَجْرَيْتَ عَلَيَّ حُكْمًاۨ اتَّبَعْتُ فِيْهِ هَوٰى نَفْسِيْ \nELAAHEE WA MAWLAAYA AJRAYTA A’LAYYA HUKMANIT-TABA’TO FEEHE HAWAA NAFSEE \nMy God and my Protector! You put into effect through me a decree in which I followed the caprice of my own soul\nوَ لَمْ اَحْتَرِسْ فِيْهِ مِنْ تَزْيِيْنِ عَدُوِّيْ \nWA LAM AH’TARIS FEEHE MIN TAZYEENE A’DUWWEE \nAnd (I) did not remain wary of adorning my enemy.\nفَغَرَّنِيْ بِمَا اَهْوٰى وَ اَسْعَدَهٗ عَلٰى ذٰلِكَ الْقَضَآءُ \nFA-GHARRANEE BEMAA AHWA WA ASA’DAHU A’LAA ZAALEKAL QAZAAA-O \nSo he deluded me through my soul’s caprice and therein destiny – favoured him \nفَتَجَاوَزْتُ بِمَا جَرٰى عَلَيَّ مِنْ ذٰلِكَ بَعْضَ حُدُوْدِكَ\nFATAJAAWAZTO BEMAA JARAA A’LAYYA MIN ZAALEKA BA’ZA HODOODEKA \nSo, in what was put into effect through me in that situation, I transgressed some of Your statutes\nوَ خالَفْتُ بَعْضَ اَوَامِرِكَ \nWA KHAALAFTO BA’ZA AWAAMEREKA \nAnd disobeyed some of Your commands.\nفَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلَيَّ فِيْ جَمِيْعِ ذٰلِكَ \nFALAKAL HAMDO A’LAYYA FEE JAMEE-E’E ZAALEKA \nPraise be to You, my Lord! You have therefore a (just) cause against me in all those matters \nوَ لَا حُجَّةَ لِيْ فِيْمَا جَرٰى عَلَيَّ فِيْهِ قَضَآؤُكَ \nWA LAA HUJJATA LEE FEE MAA JARAA A’LAYYA FEEHE QAZAAOKA \nAnd I have no plea against Your judgment passed against me.\nوَ اَلْزَمَنِيْ حُكْمُكَ وَ بَلَآؤُكَ \nWA ALZAMANI HUKMOKA WA BALAAA-OKA \nI have therefore become (justifiably) liable to Your judgment and afflictions\nوَ قَدْ اَتَيْتُكَ يَآ اِلٰهِيْ بَعْدَ تَقْصِيْرِيْ وَ اِسْرَافِيْ عَلٰى نَفْسِيْ \nWA QAD ATAYTOKA YAA ELAAHEE BA’DA TAQSEEREE WA ISRAAFEE A’LAA NAFSEE \nNow I have come to You, my Lord, after my shortcomings and transgressions against my soul,\nمُعْتَذِرًا نَادِمًا مُنْكَسِرًا مُسْتَقِيْلًا \nMO’ TAZERAN NAADEMAN MUNKASERAN MUSTAQEELAN \nProffering my excuse, regretful, broken-hearted, apologising.\nمُسْتَغْفِرًا مُنِيْبًا مُقِرًّا مُّذْعِنًا مُعْتَرِفًا \nMUSTAGHFERAN MONEEBAN MOQIRRAN MUZE’NAN MO’-TAREFAN \nAsking forgiveness, repenting, acknowledging, submissive, confessing.\nلَا اَجِدُ مَفَرًّا مِمَّا كَانَ مِنِّيْ \nLAA AJEDO MAFARRAN MIMMAA KAANA MINNEE \nI find no place to flee from what occurred through me.\nوَ لَا مَفْزَعًا اَتَوَجَّهُ اِلَيْهِ فِيْ اَمْرِيْ \nWA LAA MAFZA-A’N ATAWAJJAHO ELAYHE FEE AMREE \nNor any place of escape to which I may turn in my affairs.\nغَيْرَ قَبُوْلِكَ عُذْرِيْ وَ اِدْخَالِكَ اِيَايَ فِيْ سَعَةِ رَحْمَتِكَ \nGHAYRA QABOOLEKA U’ZREE WA IDKHAALEKA IYYAAYA FEE SA-A’TE RAH’MATEKA \nOther than Your acceptance of my excuse and Your entering me into the compass of Your mercy.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاقْبَلْ عُذْرِيْ \nALLAAHUMMA FAQBAL U’ZREE \nO Allah! So accept my excuse. \nوَ ارْحَمْ شِدَّةَ ضُرِّيْ وَ فُكَّنِيْ مِنْ شَدِّ وَثَاقِيْ \nWAR H’AM SHIDDATA ZURREE WA FUKKANEE MIN SHADDE WASAAQEE \nHave mercy upon the severity of my affliction and release me from the tightness of my fetters (evil deeds),\nيَا رَبِّ ارْحَمْ ضَعْفَ بَدَنِيْ \nYAA RABBIR HAM ZA’FA BADANEE \nMy Lord! Have mercy upon the weakness of my body,\nوَ رِقَّةَ جِلْدِيْ وَدِقَّةَ عَظْمِيْ \nWA RIQQATA JILDEE WA DIQQATA A’ZMEE \nthe delicacy of my skin and the brittleness of my bones.\nيَا مَنْۢ بَدَاَ خَلْقِيْ وَ ذِكْرِيْ \nYAA MAN BADA-A KHALQEE WA ZIKREE \nO You Who gave rise to my creation, to the remembrance of me, \nوَ تَرْبِيَتِيْ وَ بِرِّىْ وَ تَغْذِيَتِيْ \nWA TARBEYATEE WA BIRREE WA TAGHZEYATEE \nto the nurture of me, to goodness toward me and to nourishment on me.\nهَبْنِيْ لِابتِدَآءِ كَرَمِكَ وَ سَالِفِ بِرِّكَ بِيْ \nHABNEE LIB-TEDAA-E KARAMEKA WA SAALEFE BIRREKA BEE \n (I beg You) to restore Your favours and blessings upon me as You did in the beginning of my life\nيَا اِلٰهِيْ وَسَيِّدِيْ وَ رَبِّيْ \nYAA ELAAHEE WA SAYYEDEE WA RABBEE \nO Allah, my Master and my Lord!\nاَ تُرَاكَ مُعَذِّبِيْ بِنَارِكَ بَعْدَ تَوْحِيْدِكَ \nATORAAKA MOA’ZZEBEE BE-NAAREKA BA’DA TAWHEEDEKA \nWhat! Will you torment me with Your fire after I have professed Your Unity?\nوَ بَعْدَ مَا انْطَوٰى عَلَيْهِ قَلْبِيْ مِنْ مَعْرِفَتِكَ \nWA BA’DA MAN TAWAA A’LAYHE QALBEE MIN MA’REFATEKA \nAnd after my heart has embraced knowledge of You\nوَ لَهِجَ بِهٖ لِسَانِيْ مِنْ ذِكْرِكَ \nWA LAHEJA BEHEE LESAANEE MIN ZIKREKA \nAnd when my tongue has constantly praised You\nوَ اعْتَقَدَهٗ ضَمِيْرِيْ مِنْ حُبِّكَ \nWA’ TAQADAHU ZAMEEREE MIN HUBBEKA \nAnd my conscience has clung to the love of You\nوَ بَعْدَ صِدْقِ اعْتِرَافِيْ وَ دُعَآئِيْ خَاضِعًا لِرُبُوْبِيَّتِكَ \nWA BA’DA SIDQE’ TERAAFEE WA DOA’A-EE KHAAZEA’N LEROBOOBIYYATEKA \nAnd after the sincerity of my confession and my supplication, humble before Your lordship?\nهَيْهَاتَ اَنْتَ اَكْرَمُ مِنْ اَنْ تُضَيِّعَ مَنْ رَّبَّيْتَهٗ \nHAYHAATA ANTA AKRAMO MIN AN TOZAYYE-A’ MAN RABBAYTAHU \nFar be it from You! You are more generous than to squander him whom You have nurtured.\nاَوْ تُبَعِّدَ مَنْ اَدْنَيْتَهٗ اَوْ تُشَرِّدَ مَنْ اٰوَيْتَهٗ \nAW TOBA’-E’DA MAN ADNAYTAHU AW TOSHARREDA MAN AAWAYTAHU \nOr banish him whom You have brought nigh, or drive away him whom You have given an abode\nاَوْ تُسَلِّمَ اِلَى الْبَلَآءِ مَنْ كَفَيْتَهٗ وَرَحِمْتَهٗ \nAW TOSALLEMA ELAL BALAAA-E MAN KAFAYTAHU WA RAHIMTAHU \nOr submit to tribulation him whom You have spared and shown mercy.\nوَ لَيْتَ شِعْرِىْ يَا سَيِّدِيْ وَ اِلٰهِيْ وَ مَوْلَايَ \nWA LAYTA SHE’RI YAA SAYYEDI WA ELAAHEE WA MAWLAAYA \nWould that I knew, my Master, My God and my Protector.\nاَ تُسَلِّطُ النَّارَ عَلٰى وُجُوْهٍ خَرَّتْ لِعَظَمَتِكَ سَاجِدَةً \nATOSAL-LET’UN NAARA A’LAA WOJOOHIN KHARRAT LE-A’ZAMATEKA SAAJEDANW \nWill You inflict Fire upon faces which have submissively bowed in prostration to Your greatness\nوَّ عَلٰى اَلْسُنٍ نَطَقَتْ بِتَوْحِيْدِكَ صَادِقَةً وَ بِشُكْرِكَ مَادِحَةً\nWA A’LAA ALSONIN NATAQAT BE-TAWHEEDEKA SAADEQATAN WA BE-SHUKREKA MAADEHATANW\nAnd upon tongues voicing sincerely the profession of Your Unity and giving thanks to You in praise.\nوَّ عَلٰى قُلُوْبٍۨ اعْتَرَفَتْ بِاِلٰهِيَّتِكَ مُحَقِّقَةً \nWA A’LAA QOLOOBE NE’TARAFAT BE-ELAAHIYYATEKA MOHAQQEQATANW\nAnd upon hearts acknowledging Your Divinity with conviction.\nوَّ عَلٰى ضَمَآئِرَ حَوَتْ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ بِكَ حَتّٰى صَارَتْ خَاشِعَةً \nWA A’LAA ZAMAAERA HAWAT MENAL I’LME BEKAA HATTAA SAARAT KHASHEA’-TANW\nAnd upon minds encompassing knowledge of You until they have become humble\nوَّ عَلٰى جَوَارِحَ سَعَتْ اِلٰى اَوْطَانِ تَعَبُّدِكَ طَآئِعَةً وَ اَشَارَتْ بِاِسْتِغْفَارِكَ مُذْعِنَةً\nWA A’LAA JAWAAREHA SA-A’T ELA AWTAANE TA-A’BBODEKA TAA-EA’TAN WA ASHAARAT BE ISTEGHFAAREKA MUZE’NATAN \nAnd upon bodily members speeding to the places of Your worship in obedience and beckoning for Your forgiveness in submission.\nمَا هٰكَذَا الظَّنُّ بِكَ وَ لَآ اُخْبِرْنَا بِفَضْلِكَ عَنْكَ يَا كَرِيْمُ \nMAA HAAKAZAZ ZANNO BEKA WA LAA UKHBIRNA BE FAZLEKA A’NKA YAA KAREEMO \nSuch is not expected from You! Nor has such been reported – concerning You. O All- generous!\nيَا رَبِّ وَ اَنْتَ تَعْلَمُ ضَعْفِيْ عَنْ قَلِيْلٍ مِّنْۢ بَلَآءِ الدُّنْيَا وَ عُقُوْبَاتِهَا \nYAA RABBE WA ANTA TA’LAMO ZA’FI A’N QALEELIN MIN BALAA-ID DUNYA WA O’QOOBAATEHA \nMy Lord, and You know my weakness to bear even a little of this world's tribulations and punishments.\nوَ مَا يَجْرِيْ فِيْهَا مِنَ الْمَكَارِهِ عَلٰى اَهْلِهَا \nWA MAA YAJREE FEEHA MENAL MAKAAREHE A’LAA AHLEHAA \nAnd to bear those ordeals which befall its inhabitants.\nعَلٰى اَنَّ ذٰلِكَ بَلَآءٌ وَ مَكْرُوْهٌ قَلِيْلٌ مَّكْثُهٗ يَسِيْرٌ بَقَاؤُهٗ قَصِيْرٌ مُّدَّتُهٗ \nA’LAA ANNA ZAALEKA BALAAUN WA MAKROOHUN QALEE-LUN MAKSOHU YASEERUN BAQAAA-OHU QASEERUN MUDDATOHU \nEven though such tribulations and ordeals are momentary, short-lived and transient\nفَكَيْفَ احْتِمَالِيْ لِبَلَآءِ اْلآخِرَةِ وَ جَلِيْلِ وُقُوْعِ الْمَكَارِهِ فِيْهَا \nFA-KAYFA EHTEMAALEE LE BALAAA-IL AAKHERATE WA JALEELE WOQOOI’L MAKAAREHE FEEHA \nSo how can I endure the tribulations of the next world and the great ordeals that occur within it?\nوَ هُوَ بَلَآءٌ تَطُوْلُ مُدَّتُهٗ وَ يَدُوْمُ مَقَامُهٗ وَ لَا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْ اَهْلِهٖ \nWA HOWA BALAAAUN TATOOLO MUDDATOHU WA YADOOMO MAQAAMOHU WA LAA YOKHAF-FAFO A’N AHLEHI\nFor it is a tribulation whose period is long, whose station endures and whose sufferers are given no respite.\nلِاَنَّهٗ لَا يَكُوْنُ اِلَّا عَنْ غَضَبِكَ وَ اْنتِقَامِكَ وَ سَخَطِكَ \nLE-ANNAHU LAA YAKOONO ILLAA A’N GHAZABEKA WAN TEQAAMEKA WA SAKHATEKA \nSince it only occurs as a result of Your wrath, Your vengeance and Your anger.\nوَ هٰذَا مَا لَا تَقُوْمُ لَهُ السَّمٰوَاتُ وَ الْاَرْضُ \nWA HAAZA MAA LAA TAQOOMO LAHUS SAMAAWAATO WAL ARZO \nAnd these cannot be withstood by the heavens and the earth.\nيَا سَيِّدِيْ فَكَيْفَ لِيْ وَ اَنَا عَبْدُكَ الضَّعِيْفُ الذَّلِيْلُ الْحَقِيْرُ الْمِسْكِيْنُ الْمُسْتَكِيْنُ \nYAA SAYYEDI FA KAYFA BEE WA ANAA A’BDOKAZ ZAE’EFUZ ZALEELUL HAQEERUL MISKEENUL MUSTAKEENO \nO Master! So what about me?! For I am Your weak, lowly, base, wretched and miserable servant.\nيَا اِلٰهِيْ وَ رَبِّيْ وَ سَيِّدِيْ وَ مَوْلَايَ \nYAA ELAAHEE WA RABBEE WA SAYYEDEE WA MAWLAAYA \nMy God! My Lord! My Master! My Protector! \nلِاَيِّ الْاُمُوْرِ اِلَيْكَ اَشْكُوْ \nLE-AYYIL OMOORE ELAYKA ASHKOO \nFor which things would I complain to You? \nوَ لِمَا مِنْها اَضِجُّ وَ اَبْكِيْ \nWA LEMA MINHAA AZIJJO WA ABKEE \nAnd for which would I lament and weep?\nلِاَلِيْمِ الْعَذَابِ وَ شِدَّتِهٖ \nLE-ALEEMIL A’ZAABE WA SHIDDATEHI \nFor the pain and severity of chastisement?\nاَمْ لِطُوْلِ الْبَلَآءِ وَ مُدَّتِهٖ\nAM LE-TOOLIL BALAAA-E WA MUDDATEHI \nOr for the length and period of tribulation?\nفَلَئِنْ صَيَّرْتَنِىْ لِلْعُقُوْبَاتِ مَعَ اَعْدَائِكَ \nFALA-IN SAYYARTANEE LIL-O’QOOBAATE MA’A AA’DAAA-EKA \nSo if You subject me to the penalties {of hell) in company of Your enemies\nوَ جَمَعْتَ بَيْنِيْ وَ بَيْنَ اَهْلِ بَلَآئِكَ \nWA JAMA’TA BAYNEE WA BAYNA AHLE BALAAA-EKA \nAnd cast me with those who merited Your punishments\nوَ فَرَّقْتَ بَيْنِيْ وَ بَيْنَ اَحِبَّآئِكَ وَ اَوْلِيَآئِكَ \nWA FARRAQTA BAYNEE WA BAYNA AHIBBAAA-EKA WA AWLEYAAA-EKA \nAnd separate me from Your friends and saints,\nفَهَبْنِيْ يَا اِلٰهِىْ وَ سَيِّدِيْ وَ مَوْلَايَ وَ رَبِّيْ صَبَرْتُ عَلٰى عَذَابِكَ \nFAHABNEE YAA ELAAHEE WA SAYYEDEE WA MAWLAAYA WA RABBEE SABARTO A’LAA A’ZAABEKA \nThen suppose. My God, my Master, my Protector and my Lord that I am able to endure Your chastisement.\nفَكَيْفَ اَصْبِرُ عَلٰى فِرَاقِكَ\nFA-KAYFA ASBERO A’LAA FERAAQEKA \nHow can I endure separation from You?\nوَ هَبْنِيْ  صَبَرْتُ عَلٰى حَرِّ نَارِكَ \nWA HABNEE SABARTO A’LAA HARRE NAAREKA \nAnd suppose that I am able to endure the heat of Your fire,\nفَكَيْفَ اَصْبِرُ عَنِ النَّظَرِ اِلٰى كَرَامَتِكَ \nFA-KAYFA ASBERO A’NIN NAZARE ELAA KARAAMATEKA \nHow can I endure not gazing upon Your generosity?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ اَسْكُنُ فِي النَّارِ وَ رَجَآئِيْ عَفْوُكَ \nAM KAYFA ASKONO FIN NAARE WA RAJAAA-EI A’FWOKA \nOr how can I dwell in the Fire while my hope is Your pardon?\nفَبِعِزَّتِكَ يَا سَيِّدِىْ وَ مَوْلَايَ \nFA-BE-I’ZZATEKA YAA SAYYEDEE WA MAWLAAYA \nSo by Your might, my Master and protector.\nاُقْسِمُ صَادِقًا لَّئِنْ تَرَكْتَنِيْ نَاطِقًا \nUQSEMO SAADEQAN LA-IN TARAKTANEE NAATEQAN\nI swear sincerely, if You leave me with speech.\nلَاَضِجَّنَّ اِلَيْكَ بَيْنَ اَهْلِهَا ضَجِيْجَ اْلآمِلِيْنَ \nLA-AZIJJANNA ELAYKA BAYNA AHLEHA ZAJEEJAL AAMELEENA \nI will lament to You from the midst of the Fire's inhabitants with lamentation of the hopeful;\nوَ لَاَصْرُخَنَّ اِلَيْكَ صُرَاخَ الْمَسْتَصْرِخِيْنَ \nWA LA-ASROKHAN-NA ELAYKA SORAAKHAL MUSTASREKHEENA \nI will cry to You with the cry of those crying for help;\nوَ لَاَبْكِيَنَّ عَلَيْكَ بُكَاءَ الْفَاقِدِيْنَ \nWA LA-ABKEYANNA A’LAYKA BOKAAA-AL FAAQEDEENA \nI will weep to You (for being deprived of nearness to You) with the weeping of the bereaved\nوَ لَاُنَادِيَنَّكَ اَيْنَ كُنْتَ يَا وَلِيَّ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ \nWA LA-ONAADEYAN-NAKA AYNA KUNTA YAA WALIYYAL MOA-MENEENA \nAnd I will call You, Where are You. O Friend of the believers!\nيَا غَايَةَ آمَالِ الْعَارِفِيْنَ \nYAA GHAAYATA AAMAALIL A’AREFEENA \nO Goal of the hopes of Your knowers!\nيَا غِيَاثَ الْمُسْتَغِيْثِيْنَ \nYAA GHEYAASAL MUSTAGHEESEENA \nO Aid of those who seek assistance!\nيَا حَبِيْبَ قُلُوْبِ الصَّادِقِيْنَ وَ يَا اِلٰهَ الْعَالَمِيْنَ \nYAA HABEEBA QOLOOBIS SAADEQEENA WA YAA ELAAHAL A’ALAMEENA \nO You Who are dear to the hearts of the sincere, and O Lord of the universe!\nاَفَتُرَاكَ سُبْحانَكَ يَا اِلٰهِىْ وَ بِحَمْدِكَ\nAFATORAAKA SUBHAANAKA YAA ELAAHEE WA BEHAMDEKA \nMy Lord! Glory and praise be to You, \nتَسْمَعُ فِيْهَا صَوْتَ عَبْدٍ مُسْلِمٍ \nTASMA-O’ FEEHAA SAWTA A’BDIN MUSLEMIN \nwould you hear within the Fire the voice of a servant surrendered to You.\nسُجِنَ فِيْهَا بِمُخَالَفَتِهٖ وَ ذَاقَ طَعْمَ عَذَابِهَا بِمَعْصِيَتِهٖ\nSOJENA FEEHAA BE-MUKHAALAFATEHI WA ZAAQA TA-A’MA A’ZAABEHA BE-MA’SEYATEHI \nImprisoned then: because of his violations. Tasting the favour of its torment because of his disobedience.\nوَ حُبِسَ بَيْنَ اَطْبَاقِهَا بِجُرْمِهٖ وَ جَرِيْرَتِهٖ\nWA HOBESA BAYNA AT’BAAQEHA BE-JURMEHI WA JAREERATEHI \nAnd confined within its levels because of his sin and crime.\nوَ هُوَ يَضِجُّ اِلَيْكَ ضَجِيْجَ مُؤَمِّلٍ لِرَحْمَتِكَ \nWA HOWA YAZIJJO ELAYKA ZAJEEJA MO-AMMELIN LE-RAHMATEKA \nWhile he laments to You with the lament of one hopeful for Your mercy.\nوَ يُنَادِيْكَ بِلِسَانِ اَهْلِ تَوْحِيْدِكَ \nWA YONAADEEKA BE-LESAANE AHLE TAWHEEDEKA \nAnd calls to You with the tongue of those who profess Your Unity\nوَ يَتَوَسَّلُ اِلَيْكَ بِرُبُوْبِيَّتِكَ \nWA YATAWASSALO ELAYKA BE-RUBOOBIYYATEKA \nAnd entreats You by Your lordship!\nيَا مَوْلَايَ فَكَيْفَ يَبْقٰى فِي الْعَذَابِ \nYAA MAWLAAYA FA-KAYFA YABQAA FIL A’ZAABE \nMy Protector, so how should he remain in torments, \nوَ هُوَ يَرْجُوْ مَا سَلَفَ مِنْ حِلْمِكَ \nWA HOWA YARJOO MAA SALAFA MIN HILMEKA \nwhile he has hope for Your past forbearance?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ تُؤْلِمُهُ النَّارُ \nAM KAYFA TO’-LEMOHUN NAARO \nOr how should the Fire cause him pain \nوَ هُوَ يَامُلُ فَضْلَكَ وَ رَحْمَتَكَ \nWA HOWA YAAMOLO FAZLAKA WA RAHMATAKA \nwhile he expects Your bounty and mercy?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ يُحْرِقُهٗ لَهِيْبُهَا \nAM KAYFA YAHREQOHU LEHEEBOHAA \nOr how should its flames burn him \nوَ اَنْتَ تَسْمَعُ صَوْتَهٗ وَ تَرٰى مَكَانَهٗ \nWA ANTA TASMAAO’ SAWTAHU WA TARAA MAKAANAHU \nwhile You hear his voice and see his place?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ يَشْتَمِلُ عَلَيْهِ زَفِيْرُهَا \nAM KAYFA YASHTAMELO A’LAYHE ZAFEEROHA \nOr how should its roaring flames encompass him,\nوَ اَنْتَ تَعْلَمُ ضَعْفَهٗ \nWA ANTA TA’LAMO ZA’FAHU \nwhile You know his weakness?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ يَتَقَلْقَلُ بَيْنَ اَطْبَاقِهَا \nAM KAYFA YATAQALQALO BAYNA ATBAAQEHA \nOr how should he be convulsed among its levels, \nوَ اَنْتَ تَعْلَمُ صِدْقَهٗ \nWA ANTA TA’LAMO SIDQAHU \nwhile You know his sincerity?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ تَزْجُرُهٗ زَبَانِيَتُهَا \nAM KAYFA TAZJOROHU ZABAANIYYATOHA \nOr how should its keepers torture him \nوَ هُوَ يُنَادِيْكَ يَا رَبَّهٗ \nWA HOWA YONAADEEKA YAA RABBAHU \nwhile he calls out to You, O Lord?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ يَرْجُوْ فَضْلَكَ فِىْ عِتْقِهٖ مِنْهَا فَتَتْرُكُهٗ فِيْهَا \nAM KAYFA YARJU FAZLAKA FEE I’TQEHI MINHAA FA-TATROKOHU FEEHA \nOr how should he have hope of Your bounty in freeing him from it. while You abandon him within it?\nهَيْهَاتَ مَا ذٰلِكَ الظَّنُ بِكَ \nHAYHAATA MAA ZAALEKAZ ZANNO BEKA \nNay! That is not what is expected of You, \nوَ لَا الْمَعْرُوْفُ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ \nWA LAL-MA’ROOFO MIN FAZLEKA \nnor what is well-known of Your bounty.\nوَ لَا مُشْبِهٌ لِّمَا عَامَلْتَ بِهِ الْمُوَحِّدِيْنَ مِنْ بِرِّكَ وَ اِحْسَانِكَ \nWA LAA MUSHBEHUN LEMA AA’MALTA BEHIL MOWAHHEDEENA MIN BIRREKA WA EHSAANEKA \nNor it is similar to the goodness and kindness You have shown to those who profess Your Unity.\nفَبِالْيَقِيْنِ اَقْطَعُ لَوْلَا مَا حَكَمْتَ بِهٖ مِنْ تَعْذِيْبِ جَاحِدِيْكَ \nFABIL YAQEENE AQTAO’ LAW LAA MAA HAKAMTA BEHI MIN TA’ZEEBE JAAHEDEEKA \nSo I declare with certainty that were it not for what You have deemed concerning the chastisement of Your deniers\nوَ قَضَيْتَ بِهٖ مِنْ اِخْلَادِ مُعَانِدِيْكَ \nWA QAZAYTA BEHI MIN IKHLAADE MOAA’NEDIKA \nAnd what You have foreordained concerning the everlasting home of those who stubbornly resist.\nلَجَعَلْتَ النَّارَ كُلَّهَا بَرْدًا وَّ سَلَامًا \nLAJA-A’LTAN NAARA KULLAHA BARDAN WA SALAAMAN \nYou would have made the Fire, all of it, cool and peaceful.\nوَّ مَا كَانَتْ لِاَحَدٍ فِيْهَا مَقَرًّا وَّ لَا مُقَامًا \nWA MAA KAANA LE A’HADIN FEEHA MAQARRAN WA LAA MOQAAMAN \nAnd no one would have a place of rest or abode within it.\nلٰكِنَّكَ تَقَدَّسَتْ اَسْمَآؤُكَ اَقْسَمْتَ اَنْ تَمْلَاَهَا مِنَ الْكَافِرِيْنَ\nLAA KINNAKA TAQADDASAT ASMAAA-OKA AQSAMTA AN TAMLA-AHAA MENAL KAAFEREENA \nBut You – holy are Your Names – have sworn that You will fill it with the unbelievers.\nمِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَ النَّاسِ اَجْمَعينَ \nMENAL JINNATE WANNAASE AJMAEE’NA \nBoth Jinn and men together.\nوَ اَنْ تُخَلِّدَ فِيْهَا الْمُعَانِدِيْنَ \nWA AN TOKHALLEDA FEEHAL MOA’ANEDEENA \nAnd that You will place those who stubbornly resist therein forever.\nوَ اَنْتَ جَلَّ ثَنَآؤُكَ قُلْتَ مُبْتَدِئًا وَّ تَطَوَّلْتَ بِاْلاِنْعَامِ مُتَكَرِّمًا\nWA ANTA JALLA SANAAA-OKA QULTA MUBTADE-AN WA TATAWWALTA BIL I’NA’AME MOTAKARREMAN \nAnd You – exalted be Your praise – had made manifest, out of Your generosity and kindness:\nاَفَمَنْ كَانَ مُؤْمِنًا كَمَنْ كَانَ فَاسِقًا لَّا يَسْتَوُؤْنَ \nAFAMAN KAANA MO-MENAN KAMAN KAANA FAASEQAN LAA YASTAO’ONA \n ‘What? Is one who has been a believer like one who has been ungodly? They are not equal.’\nاِلٰهِىْ وَ سَيِّدِىْ فَاَسْاَلُكَ بِالْقُدْرَةِ الَّتِىْ قَدَّرْتَهَا \nELAAHEE WA SAYYEDEE FA-ASALOKA BIL QUDRATIL LATEE QADDARTAHAA \nMy God and my Master! So I ask You by the power which You have apportioned\nوَ بِالْقَضِيَّةِ الَّتِيْ حَتَمْتَهَا وَ حَكَمْتَهَا وَ غَلَبْتَ مَنْ عَلَيْهِ اَجْرَيْتَهَا \nWA BIL-QAZIYYATIL LATEE HATAMTAHAA WA HAKAMTAHAA WA GHALABTA MAN A’LAYHE AJRAYTAHAA \nAnd by the decree which You have finalised and ordained whereby You have prevailed upon whom You have imposed it\nاَنْ تَهَبَ لِىْ فِىْ هٰذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ \nAN TAHABA LEE FEE HAAZEHIL LAYLATE \nThat You forgive in this night \nوَ فِيْ هٰذِهِ السَّاعَةِ \nWA FEE HAAZEHIS SAA-A’TE \nand at this hour\nكُلَّ جُرْمٍ اَجْرَمْتُهٗ\nKULLA JURMIN AJRAMTOHU \nEvery offence I have committed, \nوَ كُلَّ ذَنْبٍ اَذْنَبْتُهٗ\nWA KULLA ZAMBIN AZNABTOHU \nand every sin I have performed.\nوَ كُلَّ قَبِيْحٍ اَسْرَرْتُهٗ \nWA KULLA QABEEHIN ASRARTOHU \nAnd every loathsome act I have concealed, \nوَ كُلَّ جَهْلٍ عَمِلْتُهٗ \nWA KULLA JAHLIN A’MILTOHU \nand every evil I have done\nكَتَمْتُهٗ اَوْ اَعْلَنْتُهٗ \nKATAMTOHU AW AA’LANTOHU \nWhether I have hidden or announced it, \nاَخْفَيْتُهٗ اَوْ اَظْهَرْتُهٗ \nAKHFAYTOHU AW AZHARTOHU \nconcealed it or manifested it\nوَ كُلَّ سَيِّئَةٍ اَمَرْتَ بِاِثْبَاتِهَا الْكِرَامَ الْكَاتِبِيْنَ \nWA KULLA SAYYEATIN AMARTA BE ISBAATEHAL KERAAMAL KAATEBEENAL \nAnd every evil act which You have commanded the Noble Writers to record.\nالَّذِيْنَ وَكَّلْتَهُمْ بِحِفْظِ مَا يَكُوْنُ مِنِّيْ \nLAZEENA WAKKALTAHUM BE HIFZE MAA YAKUNO MINNEE \nThose whom You have appointed to record all my action\nوَ جَعَلْتَهُمْ شُهُوْدًا عَلَيَّ مَعَ جَوَارِحِيْ \nWA JA-A’LTAHUM SHOHOODAN A’LAYYA MA-A’ JAWAAREHEE \nAnd whom You have made, along with my bodily members, witnesses over me.\nوَ كُنْتَ اَنْتَ الرَّقِيْبَ عَلَيَّ مِنْ وَّرَآئِهِمْ \nWA KUNTA ANTAR RAQEEBA A’LAYYA MIN WARAAEHIM \nAnd You Yourself observed over me besides them\nوَ الشَّاهِدَ لِمَا خَفِيَ عَنْهُمْ \nWASH SHAAHEDA LEMA KHAFEYA A’NHUM \nAnd witnessed that which was hidden from them\nوَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ اَخْفَيْتَهٗ \nWA BE-RAHMATEKA AKHFAYTAHU \nBut through Your mercy You concealed it \nوَ بِفَضْلِكَ سَتَرْتَهٗ \nWA BE-FAZLEKA SATARTAHU \nand through Your bounty You veiled it.\nوَ اَنْ تُوَفِّرَ حَظِّيْ مِنْ كُلِّ خَيْرٍ اَنْزَلْتَهٗ \nWA AN TOWAFFERA HAZZEE MIN KULLE KHAYRIN ANZALTAHU \nI And I ask You) that You bestow upon me an abundant share of every good You send down, \nاَوْ اِحْسَانٍ فَضَّلْتَهٗ اَوْ بِرٍّ نَشَرْتَهٗ \nAW EHSAANIN FAZZALTAHU AW BIRRIN NASHARTAHU \nand favours that your bestow And goodness You unfold, \nاَوْ رِزْقٍ بَسَطْتَهٗ اَوْ ذَنْۢبٍ تَغْفِرُهٗ \nAW RIZQIN BASAT-TAHU AW ZAMBIN TAGHFEROHU \nand provision You expand.\nاَوْ خَطَاٍ تَسْتُرُهٗ \nAW KHATAAIN TASTOROHU \nAnd sins You forgive, and errors you cover up. \nيَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ \nYAA RABBE YAA RABBE YAA RABBE \nMy Lord! My Lord! My Lord!\nيَا اِلٰهِيْ وَ سَيِّدِيْ وَ مَوْلَايَ وَ مَالِكَ رِقِّى \nYAA ELAAHEE WA SAYYEDEE WA MAWLAAYA WA MAALEKA RIQQEE \nMy God! My Master! My Protector! Owner of my bondage!\nيَا مَنْۢ بِيَدِهٖ نَاصِيَتِىْ \nYAA MAM BE-YADEHI NAASEYATEE \nO He in who holds my destiny!\nيَا عَلِيْمًا بِضُرِّىْ وَ مَسْكَنَتِىْ \nYAA A’LEEMAN BE ZURRI WA MASKANATEE \nO He who knows my affliction and my misery! \nيَا خَبِيْرًا بِفَقْرِىْ وَ فَاقَتِىْ \nYAA KHABEERAN BE FAQREE WA FAAQATEE \nHe who is aware of my poverty and indigence!\nيَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ \nYAA RABBE YAA RABBE YAA RABBE \nMy Lord! My Loid! My Lord!\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِحَقِّكَ وَ قُدْسِكَ وَ اَعْظَمِ صِفَاتِكَ وَ اَسْمَآئِكَ \nASALOKA BE HAQQEKA WA QUDSEKA WA AA’ZAME SEFAATEKA WA ASMAAEKA \nI ask You by Your Truth and Your Holiness and the greatest of Your Attributes and Names,\nاَنْ تَجْعَلَ اَوْقَاتِيْ مِنَ اللَّيْلِ وَ النَّهَارِ بِذِكْرِكَ مَعْمُوْرَةً \nAN TAJA’LA AWQAATEE MENAL LAYLE WAN NAHAARE BEZIKREKA MA’MOORATAN \nThat You make my times in the night and the day inhabited by Your remembrance.\nوَّ بِخِدْمَتِكَ مَوْصُولَةً \nWA BE KHIDMATEKA MAWSOOLATAN \nBy engaging myself in serving You (Your cause) \nوَّ اَعْمَالِىْ عِنْدَكَ مَقْبُوْلَةً \nWA AA’MAALEE I’NDAKA MAQBOOLATAN \nand to let my deeds Ire such as to be acceptable to You.\nحَتّٰى تَكُوْنَ اَعْمَالِيْ وَ اَوْرَادِىْ كُلُّهَا وِرْدًا وَّاحِدًا \nHATTA TAKOONA AA’MAALEE WA AWRAADI KULLOHA WIRDAN WAAHEDAN \nSo that my actions and offerings may be transformed into one continuous and sustained effort\nوَّ حَالِىْ فِىْ خِدْمَتِكَ سَرْمَدًا \nWA HAALEE FEE KHIDMATEKA SARMADAN \nAnd my life may take the form of constant and perpetual service to You\nيَا سَيِّدِيْ يَا مَنْ عَلَيْهِ مُعَوَّلِيْ \nYAA SAYYEDEE YAA MAN A’LAYHE MOA’WWALEE\nMy Master! O He upon whom I depend!\nيَا مَنْ اِلَيْهِ شَكَوْتُ اَحْوَالِيْ \nYAA MAN ELAYHE SHAKAWTO AHWAALEE \nO He unto Whom I express my distress! \nيَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ \nYAA RABBE YAA RABBE YAA RABBE \nMy Lord! My Loid! My Lord!\nقَوِّ عَلٰى خِدْمَتِكَ جَوَارِحِىْ \nQAWWE A’LAA KHIDMATEKA JAWAAREHEE \nStrengthen my bodily members in Your service. \nوَ اشْدُدْ عَلَى الْعَزِيْمَةِ جَوَانِحِيْ \nWASH DUD A’LAL A’ZEEMATE JAWAANEHEE \nAnd fortify my ribs to persevere in Your service\nوَ هَبْ لِيَ الْجِدَّ فِيْ خَشْيَتِكَ \nWA HAB LEYAL JIDDA FEE KHASHYATEKA \nAnd bestow upon me earnestness in my fear of You\nوَ الدَّوَامَ فِيْ الْاِتِّصَالِ بِخِدْمَتِكَ \nWAD DAWAAMA FIL ITTESAALE BE KHIDMATEKA \nAnd continuity in my being joined to Your service\nحَتّٰى اَسْرَحَ اِلَيْكَ فِيْ مَيَادِيْنِ السَّابِقِيْنَ \nHATTAA ASRAHA ELAYKA FEE MAYAADEENIS SAABE-QEENA \nSo that I may move easily toward You in the battlefields of the foremost\nوَ اُسْرِعَ اِلَيْكَ فِي الْبَارِزِيْنَ \nWA USRE-A’ ELAYKA FIL BAAREZEENA \nand be swift towards You among those who hasten towards You\nوَ اَشْتَاقَ اِلٰى قُرْبِكَ فِي الْمُشْتَاقِيْنَ \nWA ASH-TAAQA ELA QURBEKA FIL MUSHATAAQEENA \nAnd desire fervently Your proximity among the fervently desirous\nوَ اَدْنُوَ مِنْكَ دُنُوَّ الْمُخْلِصِيْنَ \nWA ADNO-A MINKA DONUWWAL MUKHLESEENA \nAnd move nearer to You with the nearness of the sincere\nوَ اَخَافَكَ مَخَافَةَ الْمُوْقِنِيْنَ \nWA AKHAAFAKA MAKHAAFATAL MOOQENEENA \nAnd fear You with the fear of those who have certitude\nوَ اَجْتَمِعَ فِىْ جِوَارِكَ مَعَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ \nWAJ TAMEA’ FEE JAWAAREKA MA-A’L MOMENEENA \nAnd gather with the believers in Your vicinity.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ مَنْ اَرَادَنِيْ بِسُوْٓءٍ فَاَرِدْهُ \nALLAAHUMMA WA MAN ARAADANEE BE SOOO-IN FA-ARIDHO \nO Allah! Whoever desires evil for me, desire [it] for him! \nوَ مَنْ كَادَنِيْ فَكِدْهُ \nWA MAN KAADANEE FAKIDHO \nAnd frustrate him who plots against me\nوَ اجْعَلْنِيْ مِنْ اَحْسَنِ عَبِيْدِكَ نَصِيْبًا عِنْدَكَ \nWAJ A’LNI MIN AH’SANE A’BEEDEKA NASEE-BAN I’NDAKA \nAnd make me one of the most excellent of Your servants in Portion from You.\nوَ اَقْرَبِهِمْ مَنْزِلَةً مِنْكَ \nWA AQRABEHIM MANZELATAM MINKA \nAnd the nearest of them in station to You\nوَ اَخَصِّهِمْ زُلْفَةً لَدَيْكَ \nWA AKHASSEHIM ZULFATAN LADAYKA \nAnd the most elected of them in proximity to You.\nفَاِنَّهٗ لَا يُنَالُ ذٰلِكَ اِلَّا بِفَضْلِكَ \nFA-INNAHU LAA YANAALO ZAALEKA ILLA BE-FAZLEKA \nFor that cannot be attained except by Your bounty.\nوَجُدْ لِيْ بِجُوْدِكَ وَ اعْطِفْ عَلَيَّ بِمَجْدِكَ \nWA JUD LEE BEJOODEKA WA’ TIF A’LAYYA BE-MAJDEKA \nAnd treat me benevolently, and through Your greatness extend Your munificence towards me\nوَ احْفَظْنِيْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ \nWAH FAZNEE BE-RAHMATEKA \nand through Your mercy protect me\nوَ اجْعَلْ لِّسَانِىْ بِذِكْرِكَ لَهِجًا وَّ قَلْبِيْ بِحُبِّكَ مُتَيَّمًا \nWAJ-A’L LESAANEE BE ZIKREKA LAHEJAN WA QALBI BE-HUBBEKA MUTAYYAMAN \nAnd make my tongue remember You without ceasing and my heart enthralled by Your love!\nوَّ مُنَّ عَلَيَّ بِحُسْنِ اِجَابَتِكَ \nWA MUNNA A’LAYYA BE-HUSNE EJAABATEKA \nAnd be gracious to me by answering me favourably.\nوَ اَقِلْنِيْ عَثْرَتِيْ وَ اغْفِرْ زَلَّتِيْ \nWA AQILNEE A’SRATEE WAGH FIR ZALLATEE \nAnd nullify my slips and forgive my lapses!\nفَاِنَّكَ قَضَيْتَ عَلٰى عِبَادِكَ بِعِبَادَتِكَ \nFA-INNAKA QAZAYTA A’LAA E’BAADEKA BE-E’BAADATEKA \nFor You have decreed Your worship for Your servants\nوَ اَمَرْتَهُمْ بِدُعَآئِكَ \nWA AMARTAHUM BE-DOA’AEKA \nAnd commanded them to supplicate You\nوَ ضَمِنْتَ لَهُمُ اْلاِجَابَةَ \nWA ZAMINTA LAHOMUL EJAABATA \nAnd assured them that they would be answered.\nفَاِلَيْكَ يَا رَبِّ نَصَبْتُ وَجْهِيْ \nFA-ELAYKA YAA RABBE NASABTO WAJHEE \nSo toward You. my Lord. I have turned my face\nوَ اِلَيْكَ يَا رَبِّ مَدَدْتُ يَدِيْ \nWA ELAYKA YAA RABBE MADADTO YADEE \nAnd toward You. my Lord. I have extended my hand.\nفَبِعِزَّتِكَ اسْتَجِبْ لِيْ دُعَآئِيْ \nFABE I’ZZATEKAS TAJIB LEE DOA’AEE \nSo by Your might, respond to my supplication\nوَ بَلِّغْنِيْ مُنَايَ وَ لَا تَقْطَعْ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ رَجَآئِيْ \nWA BALLIGHNEE MONAAYA WA LAA TAQTA-A’ MIN FAZLEKA RAJAAA-EE \nAnd make me attain my desires! Do not severe my hoping for Your Favours\nوَ اكْفِنِيْ شَرَّ الْجِنِّ وَ اْلاِنْسِ مِنْ اَعْدَآئِيْ \nWAK FENEE SHARRAL JINNE WAL INSE MIN AA’DAA-EE\nAnd spare me the evil of my enemies from among the jinn and men!\nيَا سَرِيْعَ الرِّضَا اِغْفِرْ لِمَنْ لَّا يَمْلِكُ اِلَّا الدُّعَآءَ \nYAA SAREEA’R REZAA IGH FIR LEMAN LAA YAMLEKO ILLAD DOA\nO He, Whose pleasure is quickly achieved! Forgive him who owns nothing but supplication\nفَاِنَّكَ فَعَّالٌ لِمَا تَشَآءُ \nFA INNAKA FA’-A’ALUN LEMAA TASHAAA\nFor You do what You will.\nيَا مَنِ اسْمُهٗ دَوَآءٌ وَ ذِكْرُهٗ شِفَآءٌ \nYAA MAN ISMOHU DAWAAA-UN WA ZIKROHU SHEFAAA-UN \nO He whose Name is a remedy (for all ills). And whose remembrance is a cure (for all ailments).\nوَ طَاعَتُهٗ غِنًى اِرْحَمْ مَنْ رَاْسُ مَالِهِ الرَّجَآءُ \nWA TA-A’TOHU GHENAN IRHAM MAN RAASO MAALEHIR RAJAAA-O \nAnd obedience to Whom makes one self-sufficient; Have mercy upon him whose only asset is hope\nوَ سِلَاحُهُ الْبُكَآءُ \nWA SELAA-HOHUL BOKAAA-O \nAnd whose only weapon is lamentation! \nيَا سَابِغَ النِّعَمِ \nYAA SAABEGHAN NEA’ME \nO You, Who perfects all bounties!\nيَا دَافِعَ النِّقَمِ يَا نُوْرَ الْمُسْتَوْحِشِيْنَ فِي الظُّلَمِ \nYAA DAAFE-A’N NEQAME YAA NOORAL MUSTAWHESHEENA FIZ ZOLAME \nAnd Who wards off all misfortunes! O Light! Who illuminates those who are in bewilderment!\nيَا عَالِمًا لَّا يُعَلَّمُ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nYAA A’ALEMAN LAA YO-A’LLAMO SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nO Omniscient! Who knows without (acquisition of) learning! Bless Muhammad and Muhammad’s household!\nوَّ افْعَلْ بِيْ مَا اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ \nWAF A’L BEE MAA ANTA AHLOHU \nAnd do unto me in accordance with that which befits You \nوَ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِهٖ \nWA SALLAL LAAHO A’LAA RASOOLEHI \nand blessings of Allah be on His messenger \nوَ الْاَئِمَّةِ الْمَيَامِيْنَ مِنْ آلِهٖ\nWAL A-IMMATIL MAYAAMEENA MIN AALEHI \nand the blessed guides from his household \nوَ سَلَّمَ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا.\nWA SALLAMA TASLEEMAN KASEERAA.\nand give them abundant peace!"
}
